# `-R . twarith' covers `threewords/' as well, so the paper's own development
# is built under `twarith.threewords' and needs no line of its own.  Giving it
# one binds the directory twice, and then whichever mapping is read second
# wins: read first, native compilation cannot find it; read second, nothing
# can.  Build it before this: `cd threewords && make'.
-R . twarith

# Double words.  Build code/ddouble first: `tw_ops.v' takes the float-to-real
# bridge from its `dwbridge.v', and the bench files compare against it.
-Q ../ddouble dwarith

# Triple words on primitive floats.
twarith.v
tw_updn.v
twbound.v
twpaper.v
twseed.v
twflx.v
tw_ops.v
tw_cmpbad.v
test_pi.v
tw_unsafe.v
